// The standing negative control for 07-VERIFICATION.md's PVG-01 and
// 07-REVIEW.md's CR-01. Before 07-11, this program was admitted
// `status: pass`, exit 0, zero diagnostics, by BOTH `check` and
// `corevalidate`: the call boundary neither moved nor copy-checked its
// argument, so the same non-copyable `Buffer` could be passed by value to
// two separate calls with no refusal at all.
//
// The refusal below is an OWNERSHIP refusal, not a type refusal (both
// calls' argument and parameter types match) and not a callability
// refusal (`identity` is callable -- it has no problems reported by
// originvalidate.PublishProblemsFor). The matched non-call control -- the
// identical double use written as plain bindings -- has always been
// refused with ownership.transfer_requires_take; this fixture proves the
// same law now reaches the call boundary too, via the EXISTING
// ownership.use_after_move gate.
//
// This fixture must NEVER be added to any list that expects a clean
// check, in the same way cycle_self.lang never is.

module phase07.call_argument_used_twice

export {
  fn main
}

fn identity(value: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  value
}

fn main(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let first = identity(buffer)
  let second = identity(buffer)
  second
}
